{{Top}}
{{Youmayredirect|Father|Mortis god|Father (Mortis)}}
{{Quote|If Luke couldn't reach him, how could I?''"<br />"''Luke is a Jedi. You're his father.|Han Solo and Leia Organa, about their son, Ben Solo|<ref name="Episode 7">{{Film|VII}}</ref>}}
[[File:Bridger_family.png|thumb|right|180px|A young [[Ezra Bridger]] with his parents, [[Mira Bridger|Mira]] and [[Ephraim Bridger]]]]
A '''parent''' was the [[DNA|biological]] progenitor of an offspring, or someone who looked after a person in the same way that a parent did, typically via adoption.

==Biological parents==
{{Quote|Leia, do you remember your mother, your real mother?|Luke Skywalker, to Leia Organa|<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref>}}
[[File:Midwife_droid_1.png|thumb|left|280px|Padmé Amidala gives birth to twins, Luke and Leia.]]
A [[DNA|biological]] parent, or birth parent, was the biological progenitor of an offspring.<ref name="Family at War">''[[Skywalker: A Family at War]]''</ref> Among some [[species]], such as [[human]]s, the act of becoming a parent often involved a being [[Reproduction|conceiving]] a [[Youngling|child]] with a partner,<ref name="Queen's Shadow">''[[Queen's Shadow]]''</ref> as biological parents;<ref name="Leia, Princess of Alderaan">''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]''</ref> with one person fulfilling the role of mother,<ref name="Destiny">{{Acolyte|Destiny (The Acolyte)}}</ref><ref name="Episode I">{{Film|I}}</ref> who carried the child and gave birth;<ref name="Episode I" /> and the other that of father.<ref name="Destiny" /><ref name="Episode I" /> Humans were also capable of having [[hybrid]] children with members of certain other species: For example, the female [[Twi'lek]] [[Hera Syndulla]] became a mother after she gave birth to the son of [[Kanan Jarrus]], [[Jacen Syndulla|Jacen]].<ref name="Family Reunion – and Farewell">{{Rebels|Family Reunion &ndash; and Farewell}}</ref>

[[Anakin Skywalker]], a [[Jedi]] who became known as the "[[Chosen One]]," had no known father, resulting in [[Shmi Skywalker Lars|Shmi Skywalker]]'s great surprise when she became pregnant with him. The [[Jedi Master]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]], upon being told this, speculated that Skywalker had, in fact, been conceived directly by [[midi-chlorian]]s.<ref name="Episode I" />

In some animals like [[fathier]]s, the male parent was referred to as the "sire," and the female parent as the "dam."<ref name="RT:RF">''[[The Last Jedi: Rose Tico: Resistance Fighter]]''</ref>

Some people chose to have a child without a partner, such as [[Sola Naberrie]], who delivered a daughter, [[Ryoo Naberrie]]. Sola was uninterested in having a partner, though she was comfortable with having children, a position not uncommon on her [[homeworld]] [[Naboo]].<ref name="Queen's Shadow"/> The famed [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Jango Fett]] became a parent by requesting an unaltered genetic replication of himself from [[Kaminoan]]s [[Cloning|cloners]], which resulted in the clone [[Boba Fett]], who was raised by Jango as his own son.<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref>

==Creation==
[[File:AnakinLeavesHome-CGSWG.png|thumb|200px|right|Anakin Skywalker was conceived by the Force and had no other parent than his mother, Shmi.]]
The human [[twin]] children [[Mae-ho Aniseya|Mae-ho]] and [[Verosha Aniseya]] had no father; they were created by [[Aniseya]], the leader of a [[Brendok coven|coven]] of [[witch]]es,<ref name="Destiny">{{Acolyte|Destiny (The Acolyte)}}</ref> through a powerful [[Vergence|Force vergence]] on the [[planet]] [[Brendok]].<ref name="The Acolyte">{{Acolyte|The Acolyte (episode)}}</ref> The two were then carried until their birth by Aniseya's partner [[Koril]]. Aniseya and Koril raised the sisters together as their mothers.<ref name="Destiny" />

On [[Dathomir]], the [[Dathomirian]] [[witch]] [[Falta]] used [[magick]] to create for herself a daughter, [[Yenna]], within a pod that served as the opposite of a [[burial pod]]. Falta refused to tell [[Mother (title)|Mother]] [[Talzin]], leader of the [[Nightsisters]], the secrets of her daughter's creation.<ref name="Bug">{{StoryCite|story=Bug (short story)|book=The Clone Wars: Stories of Light and Dark}}</ref>

==Adoption==
{{Quote|You really love the boy. Like he's your own.''"<br />"''He ''is'' my own.|Reva Sevander and Owen Lars, about Owen's step-nephew Luke Skywalker|<ref name="Kenobi VI">{{Kenobi|Part VI}}</ref>}}
[[File:BailBrehaLeia-hd.png|thumb|left|250px|Leia Organa was adopted by Queen Breha and Senator Bail Organa.]]
The term "parent" could also refer to a caretaker of the offspring who was not biologically related to them:<ref name="Kenobi I">{{Kenobi|Part I}}</ref> Adoption was a process where a person assumed the parenting for another and raised the offspring of the biological parents but was not related to them. [[Queen]] [[Breha Organa]] and her [[Marriage|husband]], [[Senator]] [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]], adopted the newborn [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] after Leia's biological mother, [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]], died in childbirth, and her birth father, Anakin Skywalker, fell to the [[dark side of the Force]].<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> Because of near-deadly injuries sustained by the queen during her [[Day of Demand]] challenges, Bail and Breha had decided not to conceive a child and strain the queen's body, and instead talked of adopting a child one day,<ref name="Leia">''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]''</ref> more specifically a baby girl.<ref name="Episode III" />

[[Luke Skywalker]], Leia's [[twin]] brother,<ref name="Episode III" /> was adopted by [[Owen Lars|Owen]] and [[Beru Whitesun Lars|Beru Lars]]<ref name="Vader 1">[[Darth Vader (2020) 1|''Darth Vader'' (2020) 1]]</ref>&mdash;Owen was Luke's father's step-brother.<ref name="Episode II" /> Owen was initially reluctant to take in Luke, as he had only met his step-brother once, and they were barely family and not even by blood. Another mouth to feed would also be a substantial burden for the struggling [[moisture farmer]]s. However, Beru, who was unable to have a child of her own, wished for a family and convinced her reluctant husband to adopt Anakin's son. The moment the infant Luke was placed in her arms, Beru was smitten and loved the child as if he were her own. Owen grew to care for the boy in his own gruff way.<ref name="Family at War" /> Former [[Inquisitor]] [[Reva Sevander]] noted that Owen really loved Luke, like he was his own, to which Owen replied that Luke ''was'' his own.<ref name="Kenobi VI" />

The [[Mandalorian]] [[mercenary]] [[Din Djarin]] was the caretaker of the [[foundling]] [[Din Grogu|Grogu]], and wished for his foundling to become a true Mandalorian. This led to him officially adopting Grogu as his son, as Grogu was too young to speak the [[Mandalorian Creed]], but parental consent would allow the foundling to join the [[Children of the Watch|clan]] as Djarin's [[Mandalorian apprentice]] without needing to recite the creed.<ref name="Return">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 24: The Return}}</ref>

==Parental figures==
{{Quote|A foundling is in your care. By creed, until it is of age or reunited with its own kind, you are as its father.|The Armorer, to Din Djarin|<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref>}}
[[File:PapaMando-TMUSC.png|thumb|250px|right|Din Djarin took the foundling Grogu as his son.]]
While the [[Force-sensitive]] youngling Grogu was under the care of the Mandalorian Din Djarin, [[The Armorer]] declared Grogu to be a foundling. As such, Djarin was from then on seen as Grogu's father, until Grogu was of age or Djarin returned him to his kind.<ref name="Chapter 8" /> [[Ahsoka Tano]] described Djarin as a father figure to Grogu,<ref name="Chapter 13">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 13: The Jedi}}</ref> and eventually, Djarin formally adopted him.<ref name="Return" />

[[Hunter]], a former [[clone trooper]], had taken a fatherly role with [[Omega]], one of his fellow [[Cloning|clones]] and members of [[Clone Force 99]]. As they arrived on [[Pabu]], [[Shep Hazard]] referred to Hunter as Omega's father, saying that it was a great place to raise a child.<ref name="Pabu">{{TBB|Pabu (episode)}}</ref> [[Royce Hemlock]], who was trying to kidnap Omega, was greatly surprised by how paternal Hunter acted towards her.<ref name="Order 99">{{TBB|Order 99}}</ref>

People who had no parents in their life would sometimes look for parental figures in others: [[Anakin Skywalker]], who had no known father and may have been conceived directly by [[midi-chlorian]]s,<ref name="Episode I" /> viewed his [[Jedi]] [[instructor]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] as the closest thing he had to a father.<ref name="Episode II" /> Similarly, when [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] met [[Han Solo]], she felt like he was the father she never had.<ref name="Episode VII" /> According to [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]], Rey was looking for her parents "everywhere," first in Solo, then in Luke Skywalker.<ref name="Episode VIII" /> [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], Rey's Jedi instructor, came to see Rey as the daughter she never had.<ref name="Ep IX novel">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition]]''</ref>

==Significance==
===Genetics===
{{Quote|Princess Leia Organa, you are wise, discerning, kindhearted. These are qualities that came from your mother. But you are also passionate and fearless, forthright. And these are gifts from your father. Both were exceptional people who bore an exceptional daughter.|Obi-Wan Kenobi, to Leia Organa|<ref name="Kenobi Part VI">{{Kenobi|Part VI}}</ref>}}
[[File:KyloRenHS-TFA.png|thumb|left|220px|With his father's nose and his mother's eyes, Ben Solo resembled his parents, Han Solo and Leia Organa.]]
It was possible for a child to inherit their biological parents' physical features. As a teenager, Leia Organa looked strikingly similar to her biological mother, Padmé Amidala, and when she wore the [[jubilation dress]] that Amidala had once worn it greatly shocked [[Quarsh Panaka]], an old friend and ally of Amidala's.<ref name="Leia, Princess of Alderaan" /> Organa's own son, Ben Solo, had his father Han Solo's pronounced [[nose]] and lopsided smile, and his mother's piercing [[Color|brown]] [[eye]]s. Organa, in turn, was sure that this feature was inherited from her own birth mother.<ref name="Family at War" />

Other characteristics could also be passed on from a parent to their offspring. For example, the human Force-sensitive Leia Organa was described as wise, discerning and kindhearted, like her birth mother; and passionate, fearless and forthright, like her biological father Anakin Skywalker.<ref name="Kenobi Part VI" /> Ben Solo's inherent [[The Force|Force]] ability came from his mother, whereas he gained his amazing reflexes and piloting skills from his father.<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> He also hailed from a bloodline of expert [[pilot]]s that included not only his father, but also his maternal grandfather.<ref name="TLJ Cross Sections">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: Incredible Cross-Sections]]''</ref> [[Snoke]] also claimed that Solo had "too much of his father's [[heart]]" in him, which was why he was unable to fully commit to the dark side of the Force.<ref name="Episode VIII" />

Organa's brother Luke Skywalker was known to be a great pilot, just like his father Anakin.<ref name="ANH">{{Film|IV}}</ref> He also showed an aptitude for mechanical engineering, a skill that Luke seemed to have inherited from his father, along with his father's quick reflexes and love for flying. In addition, both father and son hated living on [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Family at War" />

DNA could only be passed down genetically: The human [[Rush Clovis]] was raised in part as the adopted son of an influential [[Muun]] family on [[Scipio]], who treated him as though he were their own child. Because of how well integrated he was into Muun society, Clovis was unbothered by the fact he was a human,<ref name="Rise">{{TCW|The Rise of Clovis}}</ref> even though his species raised eyebrows to those who associated Scipio and the [[InterGalactic Banking Clan|Banking Clan]] with the Muuns.<ref name="Queen's Shadow" /> According to Clovis, he almost forgot where he was from, until he looked in the [[mirror]].<ref name="Rise" /> Despite always knowing that she was adopted, and therefore knew any shared traits were just a coincidence, as a little girl Leia Organa used to look in the mirror to see if she shared any traits with her adoptive parents such as Breha Organa's wisdom and beauty or the kindness in Bail Organa's eyes.<ref name="Leia, Princess of Alderaan" />

The saying "the [[Jogan fruit|jogan]] doesn't roll far from the vine" referred to a child taking after their parents.<ref name="Scum and Villainy">''[[Star Wars: Scum and Villainy: Case Files on the Galaxy's Most Notorious]]''</ref>

===The role of parents===
{{Quote|You sound like my parents.|Young Leia Organa, to Obi-Wan Kenobi|<ref name="Part II">{{Kenobi|Part II}}</ref>}}
[[File:Breakfast_at_Mothmas.png|thumb|right|250px|[[Mon Mothma]] and [[Perrin Fertha]] having breakfast with their daughter [[Leida Mothma|Leida]].]]
The role of a parent was associated with certain forms of behavior: For example, [[Sabine Wren]] felt that fellow [[Spectre]] member Hera Syndulla was ordering her around like she was her mother.<ref name="Sabine">''[[Sabine My Rebel Sketchbook]]''</ref> When Obi-Wan Kenobi instructed ten-year-old [[Princess]] Leia Organa on how to behave while they were trying to escape [[Daiyu]], Organa retorted that Kenobi sounded like her adoptive parents.<ref name="Part II" /> When Hunter was trying to protect Omega from being kidnapped by Royce Hemlock, the latter commented on how paternal Hunter was.<ref name="Order 99" /> When Luke Skywalker [[Duel on Cloud City|dueled]] [[Darth]] Vader on [[Bespin]], he observed Vader go from taunting him to praising him almost instantaneously, "as if he were...," yet he stopped short of finishing the thought. At the end of the duel, Luke was aghast when Vader revealed a stunning truth: that he, the man Luke believed had taken his father's life, was actually his father.<ref name="So You Want">''[[The Empire Strikes Back: So You Want to Be a Jedi?]]''</ref>

===Other significance===
{{Quote|Your parents threw you away like garbage.''"<br />"''They didn't!''"<br />"''They did. But you can't stop needing them. It's your greatest weakness.|Kylo Ren and Rey|<ref name="TLJ">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>}}
The Jedi of the [[Galactic Republic|Old Republic]] were normally taken in by the [[Jedi Order]] when they were little, with the oldest typically being no more than five [[Standard year|year]]s old. Although Jedi were not expressly forbidden from communicating with their birth parents or siblings, most of them felt little connection to their biological family because they had been inducted into the Order as infants.<ref name="Family at War" />

The revelation of one's parentage could have profound implications for an individual. Luke Skywalker was shocked upon Darth Vader, who was formerly Anakin Skywalker, telling him that he was his father.<ref name="Episode V">{{Film|V}}</ref> Although Luke did not accept this at first, he eventually came to believe it and used the information to bind them together and convince Vader to save him from the ravages of his [[Sith Master|master]], [[Darth Sidious]].<ref name="Episode VI" /> Leia Organa, the other child of Vader, was forced to exit the [[New Republic Senate|Galactic Senate]] of the [[New Republic]] upon the truth of her parentage being revealed.<ref name="Bloodline">[[Bloodline (novel)|''Bloodline'']]</ref>

[[File:DathanReyMiramir-CGSWG.png|thumb|left|250px|Rey's mother and father were forced to abandon their daughter in order to protect her.]]
Rey, an orphaned [[scavenger]] from [[Jakku]], remained on the [[planet]] in the hope that her [[Dathan|father]] and [[Miramir|mother]] would one [[Standard day|day]] return for her. Even after leaving the planet following the awakening of her [[Force power]]s,<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref> she sought desperately to learn the identity of her parents.<ref name="Episode VIII" /> Eventually, however, a journey on the planet [[Ahch-To]] and a conversation with Kylo Ren, who had killed his own father, Han Solo, led her to confront the seeming truth: that a part of her had always known that deep down that her parents were [[Junk dealer|junkers]] who sold her off for [[Alcohol|drinking]] [[Currency|money]] and were now [[Death|dead]] in a paupers' grave in the [[desert]] wastelands of Jakku.<ref name="Episode VIII">{{Film|VIII}}</ref> Further revelations, however, led her to learn that they in fact had secreted her away on Jakku in order to hide her from her [[Palpatine family|grandfather]], the [[Sith Lord]] Darth Sidious.<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

[[Loubo]], the owner of [[Plop Dribble's]], had a [[tattoo]] of a [[heart]] on his arm which said "MOM" in [[Aurebesh]].<ref name="Brothers">{{TCW|Brothers (episode)}}</ref>

